+<?php
+
+/* Members of staff see their own completed appraisals, read only */
+
+require(__DIR__ . '/includes/session.php');
+
+$Title = __('My Appraisals');// Screen identification.
+$ViewTopic = 'Labour';// Filename's id in ManualContents.php's TOC.
+$BookMark = 'MyAppraisals';// Anchor's id in the manual's html document.
+include('includes/header.php');
+include('includes/AppraisalFunctions.php');
+
+echo '<p class="page_title_text"><img alt="" src="', $RootPath, '/css/', $Theme,
+	'/images/user.png" title="',// Icon image.
+	__('My Appraisals'), '" /> ',// Icon title.
+	__('My Appraisals'), '</p>';// Page title.
+
+// Only appraisals of the employee record linked to the logged in user are ever read. Appraisals that are still open or
+// were cancelled are not shown.
+$MyEmployeeIDs = AppraisalEmployeeIDsOfUser();
+if (count($MyEmployeeIDs) == 0) {
+	prnMsg(__('Your webERP user is not linked to an employee record, so there are no appraisals to show'), 'info');
+	include('includes/footer.php');
+	exit();
+}
+$MyEmployeeList = implode(',', $MyEmployeeIDs);
+
+if (isset($_GET['AppraisalID'])) {
+	$Result = DB_query("SELECT appraisalid
+						FROM appraisals
+						WHERE appraisalid='" . (int)$_GET['AppraisalID'] . "'
+						AND employeeid IN (" . $MyEmployeeList . ")
+						AND status='" . APPRAISAL_COMPLETED . "'");
+	if (DB_num_rows($Result) == 1) {
+		echo '<div class="centre"><a href="', htmlspecialchars($_SERVER['PHP_SELF'], ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'), '">', __('Back to my appraisals'), '</a></div><br />';
+		DisplayCompletedAppraisal((int)$_GET['AppraisalID']);
+		include('includes/footer.php');
+		exit();
+	}
+	prnMsg(__('There is no such completed appraisal of yours'), 'error');
+}
+
+$TypeLabels = AppraisalTypeLabels();
+$Result = DB_query("SELECT appraisals.appraisalid,
+							appraisals.appraisaltype,
+							appraisals.completeddate,
+							appraisals.overallrating,
+							reviewers.firstname AS reviewerfirstname,
+							reviewers.surname AS reviewersurname
+					FROM appraisals
+					INNER JOIN employees AS reviewers ON appraisals.reviewerid=reviewers.id
+					WHERE appraisals.employeeid IN (" . $MyEmployeeList . ")
+					AND appraisals.status='" . APPRAISAL_COMPLETED . "'
+					ORDER BY appraisals.completeddate DESC, appraisals.appraisalid DESC");
+if (DB_num_rows($Result) > 0) {
+	echo '<table class="selection">
+		<thead>
+			<tr>
+				<th class="SortedColumn">', __('Completed'), '</th>
+				<th class="SortedColumn">', __('Type'), '</th>
+				<th class="SortedColumn">', __('Reviewer'), '</th>
+				<th class="SortedColumn">', __('Overall result'), '</th>
+				<th class="noPrint">&nbsp;</th>
+			</tr>
+		</thead>
+		<tbody>';
+	while ($MyRow = DB_fetch_array($Result)) {
+		echo '<tr class="striped_row">
+				<td>', ConvertSQLDate($MyRow['completeddate']), '</td>
+				<td>', $TypeLabels[$MyRow['appraisaltype']], '</td>
+				<td>', $MyRow['reviewerfirstname'], ' ', $MyRow['reviewersurname'], '</td>
+				<td>', AppraisalOverallText($MyRow['overallrating']), '</td>
+				<td class="noPrint"><a href="', htmlspecialchars($_SERVER['PHP_SELF'], ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'), '?AppraisalID=', $MyRow['appraisalid'], '">', __('View'), '</a></td>
+			</tr>';
+	}
+	echo '</tbody></table>';
+} else {
+	prnMsg(__('You have no completed appraisals'), 'info');
+}
+
+include('includes/footer.php');
diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..543bc19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Staff performance appraisals - notes
+
+Nothing could be run here (no shell, no database, no browser), so none of this has been executed. It was written
+against the existing code and conventions and read back by eye only. It needs a test pass on a new install, on an
+upgrade and in the browser before release.
+
+## What changed and where
+
+**Database**
+- `sql/updates/44.php` - the upgrade: new columns on `employees`, three new tables, the config value, pages,
+  security tokens, starting role assignments and menu links. Each step is re-runnable like the other updates.
+- `install/sql/tables/employees.sql` (new columns plus a foreign key to `departments`), and new
+  `appraisalcriteria.sql`, `appraisals.sql`, `appraisalscores.sql` - used by a new installation.
+- `install/sql/data/{config,scripts,securitytokens,securitygroups,menuitems}.sql` and `install/sql/demo.sql` -
+  the same rows added for a new installation (normal and demo), so new and upgraded databases match.
+- `employees` gains `departmentid`, `jobtitle`, `startdate`, `active`.
+  `appraisalcriteria` holds description, weight, job title (empty = every job title) and `retired`.
+  `appraisals` holds person, reviewer, type (1 annual, 2 mid-year), status (0 open, 1 completed, 2 cancelled),
+  dates, overall score/rating/comment. `appraisalscores` holds the rating and comment per criterion.
+- Company setting: config key `AppraisalFrequencyMonths`, default 12.
+
+**Scripts**
+- `Employees.php` - department, job title, start date and "still employed" on the staff record; list shows them;
+  delete is refused if the person has appraisals (as subject or reviewer); a person cannot be given a manager who
+  reports to them. `Departments.php` - delete is refused while employees are in the department.
+- `AppraisalCriteria.php` - criteria (add, edit, retire, use again, delete if never used) and the frequency. HR.
+- `Appraisals.php` - start an appraisal (reviewer email), list all appraisals, cancel an open one. HR.
+- `AppraisalsDue.php` - the due list with a link to start each appraisal. HR.
+- `AppraisalReview.php` - reviewer's list of waiting appraisals; rate, comment, save, complete (email to the person).
+- `MyAppraisals.php` - a member of staff's own completed appraisals, read only.
+- `includes/AppraisalFunctions.php` - shared code (scale labels, reporting chain, date reading, weighted result,
+  read-only display).
+- `doc/Manual/ManualLabour.html`, `ManualOutline.php` - manual.
+
+**Security**: new tokens 21 *Appraisals - HR administration* (criteria, frequency, start, cancel, due list),
+22 *Appraisals - reviewers*, 23 *Appraisals - own appraisals*. Starting assignment only: 21 and 22 to the roles that
+hold token 15 (system administrator), 23 to every role except the customer / supplier log-on roles. The administrator
+changes this in the usual role screens. As for every other script, the menu links are added for all roles whether or
+not the role holds the token.
+
+**Audit trail**: all writes go through `DB_query`, which already records INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE in `audittrail`, so
+appraisal changes are traced like other records. No separate mechanism was added.
+
+## Ambiguities and how I resolved them
+
+- **Who the reviewer/person are in the system.** A person is an `employees` row; "logs in" is matched through
+  `employees.userid`. A reviewer must have a webERP user (otherwise they could never do it) and must still be employed.
+  If the default manager can't qualify, HR must pick someone else above them in the line; with nobody qualifying the
+  appraisal can't be started.
+- **Existing staff have no department / job title / start date.** The columns are nullable so the upgrade works;
+  the Employees form requires all three whenever a record is saved.
+- **"Never had one" is due immediately**, including a person who started yesterday. The request has no
+  grace period for new starters, so I did not invent one.
+- **"Older than the frequency"** means last completed annual appraisal date + N months is before today (end-of-month
+  safe). Mid-year is due on or after last annual + 6 months, only if the annual one is not already due and no
+  mid-year has been completed since that annual appraisal. Due list rows show which type is due.
+- **Completion date** (not due date or start date) is what ageing uses.
+- **Rounding**: the weighted average rounds half up (3.5 -> 4). Weights must be greater than zero.
+- **Criteria for an appraisal** are worked out when the reviewer opens it/completes it: not retired, and for every job
+  title or the person's current job title (case-insensitive). Completing needs all of them rated and at least one
+  criterion. Description, weight and the job title are copied onto the completed appraisal, so later edits to a
+  criterion do not change history. Draft ratings for criteria retired meanwhile are dropped on completion.
+- **"Used in an appraisal"** = has a saved score row, including drafts and cancelled appraisals.
+- **One open appraisal per person** is enforced when starting (the due list assumes it).
+- **Cancelled/left people**: marking someone as having left does not cancel their open appraisals; HR can cancel them.
+- **Reviewers' view** is limited to appraisals waiting for them (plus a just-completed one by link). HR sees status and
+  overall result in the list but not the ratings; only the person appraised sees completed details on My Appraisals.
+- **Dates** are typed and shown in the user's `DefaultDateFormat` (text inputs, validated with `Is_Date`), stored as SQL dates.
+- **Menu**: placed in the Manufacturing module next to Employees/Timesheets, since there is no HR module.
+
+## Not done / follow-ups
+
+- The translation template (`.pot`) was not regenerated (no tooling here); all new text uses `__()`.
+- `install/sql/tables/employees.sql` keeps `stockid varchar(20)` as it was; update 43 widens it on upgrades only
+  (existing discrepancy, left alone).
+- The root `sql/` legacy dumps and `sql/mysql/` upgrade scripts were not touched.
+- The demo employees have no department/job title/start date; the form will ask for them on first edit.
diff --git a/doc/Manual/ManualLabour.html b/doc/Manual/ManualLabour.html
index f8ddce4..e02967a 100644
--- a/doc/Manual/ManualLabour.html
+++ b/doc/Manual/ManualLabour.html
@@ -50,4 +50,32 @@
 <p>Once the labour type stock category is defined any number of labour type items can be defined like any other stock item. However, since each employee is mapped to a particular labour item it is only necessary to define labour type items for each category of labour where they will have a different cost. Perhaps tradesfolk, apprentices, supervisors may be set up with different costs - but all posted in the GL on the same basis using the same labour stock category.</p>
 <p>Having set up the necessary labour stock categories and labour items in those categories, then the employees can be defined</p>
 <p align="center"><img src="doc/Manual/images/Employees.png"></p>
+<p>Each employee also has the details HR needs for appraisals: the <b>department</b> they work in (departments are set up under Departments in the set up menu), their <b>job title</b>, the <b>date they started</b> and whether they are <b>still employed</b>. Dates are entered and shown in the date format of the user. When an employee leaves, clear <i>Still Employed</i> - the record is kept, but the person is no longer due appraisals. An employee who has appraisals cannot be deleted, and neither can a department that has employees in it. The manager of an employee cannot be someone who reports to that employee.</p>
+
+<h2><a id="Appraisals">Staff Appraisals</a></h2>
+<p>Staff appraisals are done on the same employee records that are used for timesheets, so HR, managers and staff work from one place. An appraisal rates a member of staff on a list of criteria. Each criterion is rated on this scale:</p>
+<table align="center">
+<tr><td>1</td><td>Unsatisfactory</td></tr>
+<tr><td>2</td><td>Needs improvement</td></tr>
+<tr><td>3</td><td>Meets expectations</td></tr>
+<tr><td>4</td><td>Exceeds expectations</td></tr>
+<tr><td>5</td><td>Outstanding</td></tr>
+</table>
+<p>Who can do what is decided by the webERP administrator through the security roles. Three security tokens are used: <i>Appraisals - HR administration</i> (criteria, the frequency, starting and cancelling appraisals and the list of appraisals due), <i>Appraisals - reviewers</i> (doing the appraisals that are waiting) and <i>Appraisals - own appraisals</i> (seeing one's own completed appraisals). Changes to appraisals are recorded in the audit trail like changes to other records.</p>
+
+<h3>Criteria and the appraisal frequency</h3>
+<p>HR maintains the criteria under <i>Appraisal Criteria</i> in the Manufacturing maintenance menu, for example "Quality of work" or "Teamwork". Each criterion has a <b>weight</b> - how much it counts towards the overall result - and applies either to every job title (leave the job title empty) or to one job title only. A criterion that has been used in an appraisal cannot be deleted, only <i>retired</i>; a retired criterion is not used in appraisals from then on, and can be put back into use again.</p>
+<p>The same screen holds the company setting <b>months between annual appraisals</b>. It starts at 12.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="StartingAppraisals">Starting an appraisal</a></h3>
+<p>HR starts an appraisal under <i>Staff Appraisals</i>: select the member of staff, choose an annual or a mid-year appraisal and enter the date it is due. The reviewer is the person's manager unless HR chooses someone else - the reviewer must be above the person in the reporting line (their manager, their manager's manager and so on). The reviewer must still be employed and must be a webERP user. A person can only have one appraisal that is open at a time. The reviewer is told by email that the appraisal is waiting, with a link to it. HR can cancel an appraisal that has not been completed from the same screen.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="DoingAppraisals">Doing an appraisal</a></h3>
+<p>Reviewers see the appraisals waiting for them under <i>Conduct Appraisals</i>. The reviewer rates the person on each criterion that applies to their job title (the criteria that apply to every job title and those for their job title), adds a comment for each criterion and an overall comment. <i>Save</i> keeps what has been entered so that the reviewer can come back later. When the reviewer chooses <i>Complete Appraisal</i> every criterion must have been rated. The overall result is the weighted average of the ratings, rounded to the nearest point of the scale (a half rounds up), and is shown with its label, for example "4 - Exceeds expectations". Until an appraisal is completed the overall result is shown as "Not rated". A completed appraisal cannot be changed, and the person who was appraised is told by email.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="AppraisalsDue">Appraisals due</a></h3>
+<p><i>Appraisals Due</i> lists the staff who are due an appraisal: everyone still employed who has no appraisal open and whose last completed annual appraisal is older than the appraisal frequency, or who has never had one. A mid-year appraisal is due six months after the last annual appraisal. Each line has a link to start the appraisal.</p>
+
+<h3><a id="MyAppraisals">My appraisals</a></h3>
+<p>Every member of staff who logs in to webERP - and whose employee record is linked to their webERP user - can see their own completed appraisals under <i>My Appraisals</i>: the criteria, ratings, comments and the overall result. They cannot change them. Appraisals that are still open or were cancelled, and appraisals of other people, are never shown.</p>
 
